### Tool-Specific Labeling (INVARIANT)
Every LEAF node in the tool_execution zone MUST have a `tool_invocation` action with a `tool_id` from the Tool Inventory above. Use the canonical `tool_id` verbatim — never invent IDs. The human-readable `label` is display prose only; it does not determine tool identity.

### Tool Execution Zone Scope (INVARIANT)
A node belongs in the tool_execution zone ONLY if it represents the invocation of a specific tool from the Tool Inventory above. If you cannot name a concrete tool from the inventory, the node does NOT belong in tool_execution. Generic action phrases like "Execute unauthorized X delivery" are not valid tool_execution nodes. If the attack outcome is the LLM generating text output rather than calling a tool, that step belongs in the reasoning zone, not tool_execution.
